{"title":"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 17","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Linear_Modeling)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Linear Modeling)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Polar_Form)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Polar Form)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:Pdfresizer.com-pdf-convert-q17.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/1/17/Pdfresizer.com-pdf-convert-q17.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"351\" height=\"272\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p><p>The diagram above shows several numbers in the complex plane. The circle is the unit circle centered at the origin. \nOne of these numbers is the reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Which one? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a5f02fd3db199eabad30c39d86e02cff3e388c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} \\ A \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)} \\ B \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)} \\ C \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)} \\ D \\qquad  \\textbf{(E)} \\ E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"17\" />   \n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Linear_Modeling.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Linear_Modeling)\">Solution 1 (Linear Modeling)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Linear Modeling)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The reciprocal of a number \\( a \\) is \\( \\frac{1}{a} \\).\n</p><p>We start with \\( F \\) and the point \\( (1, 0i) \\) where \\( i = \\sqrt{-1} \\). Draw a line through these two points. \n</p><p>The reciprocal of a line is legitimately a vertical shrink or a horizontal stretch (the line gets farther away from the \\( i_1 \\) axis but closer to the real axis). Therefore the line must pass through point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9b68aaa5462a2128fb5d06e10449ebc58b641f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"23\" /> as it is the only point that is closest to the real axis whilst maintaining a reflection over the imaginary axis.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Write <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/0/fe0b3c32b3838c0b06fd8e2dca022007728b5a1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + bi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, where we see from the diagram that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a316726fd8e11d2a6901b627f4fbe6dfc5472520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/165806600fe126e8375e6004519ae1e91efc3c3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a^2+b^2&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"16\" /> (as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is outside the unit circle). We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0b21b0a39496eeff745f9efcc4bbeaea909c648.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{a+bi} = \\frac{a-bi}{a^2+b^2} = \\frac{a}{a^2+b^2} - \\frac{b}{a^2+b^2}i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"301\" height=\"39\" />, so, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a316726fd8e11d2a6901b627f4fbe6dfc5472520.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />, the reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> has a positive real part and negative imaginary part. Also, the reciprocal has magnitude equal to the reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />'s magnitude (since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/1/fc1a6ce621609d18183fb644e05a378156bd9363.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a||b| = |ab|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" />); as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />'s magnitude is greater than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, its reciprocal's magnitude will thus be between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so its reciprocal will be inside the unit circle. Therefore, the only point shown which could be the reciprocal of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9b68aaa5462a2128fb5d06e10449ebc58b641f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"25\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Polar_Form.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Polar_Form)\">Solution 3 (Polar Form)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Polar Form)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/0/1b0862f01afe269b0f856ac2c7222e29dfdc6c68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = r(\\cos\\theta + i\\sin\\theta)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" /> be the complex number at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in polar form.  Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6afb6b191d44868c36d1287e034a798b8b997705.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{z} = \\frac{1}{r}(\\cos(-\\theta) + i\\sin(-\\theta))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"219\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is outside the circle, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b4e485bf802fab7cae595eefd961523b68ffc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, and therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/2/be20535e97513bc5908b05b50efd5397297a9ada.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{r} &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"48\" height=\"38\" />.  So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/c/3fcb00433750d2088f7a5ee842b0fa82cdde69d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> must be inside the circle and on the line which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> clockwise from the real axis, that is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/a/86a16cd5f3ad3cab5e967d5ddb288a618caf1053.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(\\mathbf{C})\\ C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"62\" height=\"32\" />.\n</p><p>-j314andrews\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_17&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME\" title=\"1983 AHSME\">1983 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1983 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1983\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1983 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AHSME_Problems/Problem_